flowchart TB
    accTitle: Public demo — open access with read-only queries
    accDescr: Anyone can try the demonstration without logging in. The app validates a single SELECT-based query and rejects writes, deletes, and schema changes. Accepted queries run in a read-only PostgreSQL transaction and return up to 1,000 rows. Dataset seeding is separate from this query path.
    %% Companion guide: docs/security.md

    VISITOR["Public demo: Try it without a login"]:::view
    CHECK["Validate SQL: One SELECT-based query"]:::work
    REJECT["Reject writes, deletes, and schema changes"]:::note
    TRANSACTION["Execute with PostgreSQL READ ONLY"]:::work
    DB[("Read demo data")]:::data
    RESULT["Explore results: Up to 1,000 loaded rows"]:::view

    VISITOR -->|1| CHECK
    CHECK -->|2. Accepted query| TRANSACTION
    CHECK -.->|Invalid SQL| REJECT
    TRANSACTION -->|3| DB
    DB -->|4| RESULT

